Subject: cmd.exe: shell32 is loaded the first time a command needs it.

Windows' cmd.exe imports neither user32 nor shell32: the shell comes through
a delay load (ext-ms-win-shell-shell32) when start or a document needs it.
Wine's imported it, and Arctic's shell32 is ReactOS', whose comctl32 loads the
display driver in its DllMain: every cmd.exe connected to dwm.exe and read
the display configuration under the loader lock, thousands of times in a
build, and the session froze twice in the middle of that (2026-10-22).
---
diff --git a/programs/cmd/Makefile.in b/programs/cmd/Makefile.in
index cc91373..0a0948d 100644
--- a/programs/cmd/Makefile.in
+++ b/programs/cmd/Makefile.in
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 MODULE    = cmd.exe
-IMPORTS   = shell32 user32 advapi32 kernelbase
+# Windows' cmd.exe imports no shell32: it loads it the first time a command
+# needs the shell (start, a document to open), through a delay load.
+# Imported, ReactOS' shell32 brought comctl32 into every cmd.exe, and its
+# DllMain the display driver and a connection to dwm.exe, under the
+# loader lock: thousands of them in a build, each able to stall the rest.
+IMPORTS   = user32 advapi32 kernelbase
+DELAYIMPORTS = shell32
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -mconsole -municode
 
